    <!--
        REMOVED 2026-08-20: <excludeButtons>SmartFillEnrich</excludeButtons>. This line arrived
        via a RETRIEVE from usman-dpeg (commit b426598, "Retrieve Notes & Attachments onto the
        LOI, NDA and PSA Version layouts"), not hand-authored, and it blocked every subsequent
        deploy of this file with:
          "In field: excludeButtons, no such standard action: SmartFillEnrich"
        Verified safe to remove, not just to silence: SmartFillEnrich is not a QuickActionDefinition
        in this org, and - the decisive check - is absent from the full standard-action inventory
        the UI API actions endpoint returns for a live LOI__c record (Edit, LOI__c.Submit_for_Approval,
        Delete, Global.NewTask, Global.LogACall, Global.NewEvent, Global.SendEmail - no
        SmartFillEnrich). Contrast with the OpenSlackRecordChannel exclusion retained just below:
        that one deploys cleanly with no error, proving the validator DOES recognize real standard
        action names when excluded - it specifically does not recognize SmartFillEnrich as one.
        excludeButtons only ever HIDES a button; excluding one that does not exist is a no-op, so
        deleting the exclusion changes nothing a user sees.
        🔴 A future retrieve of this layout from the same org will RE-INTRODUCE this line (the org
        emits the token on retrieve even though it rejects it on deploy - a platform asymmetry).
        Whoever hits that should re-apply this same removal rather than re-investigate from
        scratch.

        ADDED 2026-08-21 (UAT unblock): Final_Agreed_Price__c to column 1, after Counter_Cap_Rate__c.
        Final_Price_Required_Before_Executed (objects/LOI__c/validationRules) blocks a disposition
        LOI moving Negotiation -> Signed with this field blank, but the field was on NEITHER this
        layout NOR LOI_Record_Page's Details tab (which renders via force:detailPanel, i.e. THIS
        layout, so fixing it here is sufficient - no flexipage edit needed). Users had no UI path
        to satisfy the rule. DPEG_Disposition_Edit already grants
        <editable>true</editable> on LOI__c.Final_Agreed_Price__c (pre-existing, confirmed in git
        history before this change - not part of this edit). This is the ONLY LOI layout, shared by
        both record types, so the field is now also visible on acquisition LOIs; it renders
        read-only there (no acquisition permission set grants it editable), which is a visibility
        change only, not a behaviour change - flagged here per standing convention, not applied
        conditionally, because a static Layout cannot express a record-type-conditional field.
    -->
